Experiment A — RNA pairing-probability analysis (58 structures)
Project 7 · RNA Bioinformatics · Université Paris-Saclay
Aim
We compared the pairing probabilities from ViennaRNA, LinearPartition-V and EternaFold with structural pairing labels derived from PDB RNA structures. The starting benchmark contained 89 structures. We excluded 31 with crossing base pairs, leaving 58 RNAs and 3,426 nucleotide positions for this analysis.

For each nucleotide, we summed its base-pair probabilities across possible partners to obtain the predicted probability of being paired. We then compared those probabilities with the reference labels using ECE (10 bins), Brier score and log loss, and plotted reliability curves. We also estimated uncertainty by resampling the benchmark's supplementary-section groups.
Running the notebook
This notebook is intended for Google Colab. Run the cells in order and upload Project7_ExperimentA_58_screening_package.zip when prompted. The input package should contain the 58-RNA FASTA, nucleotide-level reference labels and supplementary-section manifest. The original source CT records are part of the structural-reference preparation, but the prediction cells use the prepared FASTA and CSV files.

The predictor versions and settings are fixed in the cells below. Installing and compiling the tools may take time on a fresh runtime. We have saved the results of the analysis separately in the repository; this organized notebook has not been rerun from start to finish as a fresh reproducibility test.

The later 50- and 45-RNA sensitivity analyses, Rfam screening and post-hoc calibration are kept in separate files under Experiment_A/analysis/. Check data-sharing permissions before publishing the original structural reference package.


