7. Grouped bootstrap for the 58-RNA dataset
Several structures belong to the same supplementary-section grouping, so resampling individual nucleotides would give a misleading impression of independence. We therefore resampled the 35 supplementary-section groups, keeping each sampled group intact and using the same resamples for all three predictors.

This cell uses 2,000 bootstrap replicates and reports percentile 95% confidence intervals. The 45-RNA sensitivity analysis uses a separate, later 5,000-replicate bootstrap. Supplementary-section groups are a practical grouping choice, not verified evolutionary RNA families.


