Interpretation and limitations
On this 58-RNA structural reference set, we report calibration at the nucleotide level, with grouped uncertainty as a sensitivity analysis. The larger starting benchmark contained 31 structures with crossing base-pair annotations that we excluded because the prediction comparison uses a pseudoknot-free representation.

The reported results should not be described as performance on confirmed family-disjoint RNAs. The 35 supplementary-section labels are not established evolutionary-family assignments, and later Rfam screening does not prove independence from a predictor's training data.

We used ViennaRNA's partition function, LinearPartition-V with beam size 100 and EternaFold with EternaFoldParams.v1 and posterior threshold 0.00001. We assessed the effects of possible sequence overlap, duplicate records and post-hoc calibration in separate 50/45-RNA analyses.

Reproducibility note: To verify this notebook on a fresh runtime, rerun it with the documented structural inputs and compare the resulting CSVs with the saved tables in Experiment_A/results/58_RNAs/. The results should not be described as freshly reproduced until that check has been completed.
